    examFormat: "MCQ + outbreak management",
    summary: `# 🦠 Zoonoses #2.1-2.3 — Influenza A (Avian + Swine + Canine)

## 🎯 Influenza A virus
- **Family:** Orthomyxoviridae
- **Genome:** 8 segments, ssRNA negative-sense
- **Subtypes:** based on HA (H1-H18) + NA (N1-N11)
- **Antigenic drift** (point mutations) → seasonal flu
- **Antigenic shift** (reassortment) → pandemic

## 🐔 Avian influenza (AI)

### Classification
- **LPAI** (low pathogenic) — mild, asymptomatic
- **HPAI** (high pathogenic) — systemic, ~100% mortality, H5/H7

### H5N1 history
- 1997 Hong Kong — first human cases (18, 6 deaths)
- 2003-2010 — Asian outbreak, TH culled millions
- 2014 — H5N1 + H5N6 + H5N8 clades
- 2024 — H5N1 dairy cattle USA (novel!)

### Clinical (poultry)
- Sudden death (HPAI)
- Cyanotic comb/wattles
- Drop in egg production
- Neurological signs

### Human cases
- Conjunctivitis, fever, pneumonia, ARDS
- ~50% case fatality (H5N1)
- Limited human-to-human transmission (so far)

### Control
- Stamping out (cull infected flocks)
- Movement restriction
- Surveillance + reporting (WOAH list A)
- Vaccination (controversial — masks surveillance)

## 🐷 Swine influenza

### Triple reassortant (2009 H1N1 pandemic)
- Avian + human + classical swine genes
- Mexican origin
- Pandemic — millions of cases worldwide
- Now seasonal H1N1pdm09

### Pig as "mixing vessel"
- Pigs have BOTH avian (α2,3-SA) + human (α2,6-SA) receptors
- Co-infection → reassortment → novel viruses
- **Greatest pandemic risk**

## 🐶 Canine influenza
- **H3N8** — equine origin, jumped to dogs (2004 USA)
- **H3N2** — avian origin, Korea/China (2007)
- Clinical: cough, fever, pneumonia
- Vaccine available (USA)

## 🛡️ Prevention
- Biosecurity (poultry farms, pig farms)
- Vaccination (poultry, pigs)
- PPE for handlers (during outbreaks)
- Wet market hygiene
- Influenza surveillance (live bird markets, sentinel pigs)

## 🇹🇭 Thailand context
- 2004 H5N1 outbreak — major impact
- Ongoing surveillance
- DLD + Department of Livestock + DDC coordinate

## 📝 EXAM RECAP
1. ⭐ Pig = mixing vessel (both avian + human SA receptors)
2. ⭐ HPAI vs LPAI: H5/H7 polybasic cleavage site
3. ⭐ H5N1 ~50% CFR in humans
4. ⭐ 2009 H1N1 = triple reassortant pandemic
5. ⭐ Stamping out = AI control method`,
