    summary: `# 🦠 Zoonoses #2.4 — Ebola & Nipah Virus

## 🦇 Ebola virus disease (EVD)

### Pathogen
- **Family:** Filoviridae
- **Species:** Zaire (most lethal), Sudan, Tai Forest, Bundibugyo, Reston
- **Reservoir:** Fruit bats (*Pteropodidae*)

### Transmission
- Reservoir → bushmeat handling → spillover
- Human-to-human: body fluids, contact, sexual
- Healthcare-associated outbreaks common
- Funeral practices = high risk

### Clinical
- Incubation 2-21 days
- Phase 1: fever, myalgia, headache (flu-like)
- Phase 2: GI (vomiting, diarrhea)
- Phase 3: hemorrhagic (petechiae, bleeding)
- CFR: 25-90% (Zaire)

### Major outbreaks
- 1976 — first outbreaks (DRC, Sudan)
- 2014-2016 — West Africa (28,000 cases)
- 2018-2020 — DRC

### Treatment + prevention
- Supportive care
- **Inmazeb / Ebanga** — monoclonal antibodies
- **Ervebo** vaccine (rVSV-ZEBOV)
- PPE, isolation, contact tracing, safe burials

## 🦇 Nipah virus

### Pathogen
- **Family:** Paramyxoviridae, genus *Henipavirus*
- **Reservoir:** Fruit bats (*Pteropus*)

### Transmission
- Bat → date palm sap (contaminated) → human (Bangladesh)
- Bat → pig → human (Malaysia 1998-99)
- Human-to-human (limited, healthcare workers)
- **No vector**, no respiratory spread

### Clinical
- Incubation 4-14 days
- Encephalitis (50-100% in some outbreaks)
- Respiratory illness
- Mortality 40-75%

### Outbreak history
- **1998-99 Malaysia** — pig farms, 105 deaths, $$$ pig industry collapse
- **Bangladesh** — annual since 2001, date palm sap
- **India 2018** — Kerala outbreak
- **2024** — Kerala recurring

### Control
- No vaccine (animal vaccine in development)
- No specific treatment (ribavirin tried)
- Bangladesh: cover sap collection pots
- Malaysia: pig farm cull, surveillance

## 🎯 Key comparison

| Feature | Ebola | Nipah |
|---|---|---|
| Family | Filoviridae | Paramyxoviridae |
| Reservoir | Fruit bats | Fruit bats |
| Intermediate | Primates (some) | Pigs (Malaysia), date palm sap (BGD) |
| Main syndrome | Hemorrhagic fever | Encephalitis |
| Vaccine | Yes (Ervebo) | No |
| Therapy | mAb (Inmazeb) | Supportive |

## 📝 EXAM RECAP
1. ⭐ Ebola: Filoviridae, Zaire most lethal, fruit bats
2. ⭐ Nipah: Paramyxoviridae, fruit bats, encephalitis
3. ⭐ Malaysia 1998 Nipah → pigs amplifier
4. ⭐ Bangladesh Nipah → date palm sap
5. ⭐ Ervebo vaccine = Ebola; no vaccine for Nipah`,
