    examFormat: "MCQ + concept + control",
    summary: `# 🦠 Zoonoses #9 — Prion Diseases (TSEs)

## 🎯 Prion concept
- **Prion** = proteinaceous infectious particle (no nucleic acid!)
- Misfolded prion protein (PrP^Sc) catalyzes conversion of normal PrP^C
- Stanley Prusiner Nobel 1997
- Resistant to: heat (autoclave 121°C insufficient), formalin, UV, irradiation
- Inactivated by: NaOH 1N, prolonged 134°C autoclave (sterilization standards)

## 🧠 Major TSEs (Transmissible Spongiform Encephalopathies)

| Disease | Species | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Scrapie | Sheep, goat | Oldest (200+ yr), not zoonotic |
| BSE ("mad cow") | Cattle | Zoonotic → vCJD humans |
| CWD | Deer, elk | USA, Korea; potential zoonosis (concern) |
| TME | Mink | Rare |
| FSE | Cats (zoo + domestic) | BSE-linked |
| CJD | Human | Sporadic, familial, iatrogenic, variant (vCJD) |
| Kuru | Human (Papua) | Cannibalism, historic |
| GSS | Human | Familial |
| FFI | Human | Fatal familial insomnia |

## 🐄 BSE ("mad cow disease")

### History
- 1986 UK first cases — meat-and-bone meal feeding
- Peak 1992 (37,000 cases UK)
- Feed ban 1988 (UK), EU 2001
- vCJD link confirmed 1996

### Pathology
- Spongiform vacuolation in neurons
- PrP^Sc accumulation (Western blot, IHC)
- No inflammation

### Clinical (cattle)
- Behavior change (apprehension, kicking)
- Hyperesthesia
- Ataxia, falling
- Death 1-6 months after onset

### Surveillance
- Active: brainstem testing all "downer" cattle
- WOAH list, country status (free, controlled, undetermined)
- TH: BSE-free (negligible risk)

### Specified Risk Material (SRM) removal
- Brain, spinal cord, eyes, tonsils, distal ileum
- Banned from food chain in BSE countries

## 🧠 vCJD (variant CJD)
- Human form linked to BSE
- Younger patients (~28 yr median)
- Psychiatric prodrome → ataxia → dementia
- ~230 cases globally (mostly UK)
- Methionine homozygous at codon 129 (susceptibility)

## 🦌 CWD (Chronic Wasting Disease)
- Deer, elk, moose, reindeer
- USA, Canada, Korea, Norway (2016 first European)
- Spreads via saliva, urine, feces (environmental)
- Decontaminate environment difficult
- Zoonotic potential UNKNOWN (no proven cases yet)
- Concerning trend

## 🛡️ Prevention
- Feed bans (no meat-and-bone meal to ruminants)
- SRM removal
- Surveillance
- Hunter precautions (CWD)
- No cure or treatment

## 📝 EXAM RECAP
1. ⭐ Prion = misfolded PrP^Sc (no nucleic acid)
2. ⭐ BSE → vCJD humans (UK 1996)
3. ⭐ Resistant to standard sterilization
4. ⭐ SRM removal = brain, spinal cord, eyes, tonsils
5. ⭐ Feed ban (no MBM) = key prevention`,
